        "original_id": "e339db8b-5011-5b24-b4a4-3e2013694b1c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Chvrches, Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie\n- People: Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, Martin Doherty, Martin Metcalfe, John Duncan, Fin Wilson, Shirley Manson, Rona Scobie, Derek Kelly\n- Songs and Albums: \"Make Them Gold\", Every Open Eye\n- Places: Bathgate, Edinburgh, Scotland\n- Topics: band lineups, music roles\n\nFacts:\n- Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie was a Scottish rock group from the 1980s and 1990s that was formed in Bathgate near Edinburgh, Scotland.\n- Shirley Manson was a backing vocalist and keyboard player for Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie from 1981 to 1992.\n- At Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie's commercial peak, the lineup included Martin Metcalfe on vocals, John Duncan on guitar, Fin Wilson on bass guitar, Shirley Manson and Rona Scobie on keyboards and backing vocals, and Derek Kelly on drums.\n- Chvrches consists of Lauren Mayberry, Iain Cook, and Martin Doherty.\n- In Chvrches, Lauren Mayberry performs lead vocals, drums, additional synthesisers, and samplers.\n- In Chvrches, Iain Cook performs synthesisers, guitar, bass, and vocals.\n- In Chvrches, Martin Doherty performs synthesisers, samplers, and vocals.\n- \"Make Them Gold\" is a song by Chvrches from the band's second studio album Every Open Eye.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6e5acaf8-1110-5dcc-a1f7-b0d426f01107",
        "text": "Page: Chvrches. Sentence: The band consists of Lauren Mayberry (lead vocals, drums, additional synthesisers, samplers), Iain Cook (synthesisers, guitar, bass, vocals) and Martin Doherty (synthesisers, samplers, vocals).\nPage: Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie. Sentence: Goodbye Mr Mackenzie (known informally as \"The Mackenzies\") was a Scottish 1980s and 1990s rock group formed in Bathgate, near Edinburgh, Scotland.\nPage: Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie. Sentence: At the band's commercial peak, the line-up consisted of Martin Metcalfe on vocals, John Duncan on guitar, Fin Wilson on bass guitar, Shirley Manson and Rona Scobie on keyboards and backing vocals, and Derek Kelly on drums.\nPage: Make Them Gold. Sentence: \"Make Them Gold\" is a song by Scottish synthpop band Chvrches from their second studio album, \"Every Open Eye\".\nPage: Shirley Manson discography. Sentence: Before then, she was a backing vocalist and keyboard player for Goodbye Mr. Mackenzie from 1981 to 1992.",
